Additional considerations

The type field reflects the structure’s generic_type: unit (research and support units), institution, institution_subdivision, unit_subdivision, team.
main_mission and secondary_missions are only present when type is unit. They are absent for institutions, institution subdivisions, unit subdivisions, and teams.
memberships carries MEMBER_OF relationships (supervision chains for research units; org-level membership for teams and subdivisions). The position field is only set for supervision relationships (main_supervision, associated_supervision, participating_supervision).
parents carries PART_OF relationships (structural inclusion — e.g. a faculty inside a university, a team inside a research unit).
addresses and electronical_addresses are included in the schema for completeness but are currently empty in all events — contact data is not yet persisted in the graph.
The uid is the IKG-computed primary key (e.g. local-123456, uai-0751818J). It is stable for the lifetime of the structure and can be used as a join key across events.
external: false means the structure was sourced from the institution’s own directory. external: true means the structure was auto-created by IKG from the national registry because it appeared as a relationship target (e.g. a supervising institution referenced by a UAI or ROR identifier but never sent directly by the directory). Registry-created structures carry only a limited set of fields (labels, identifiers, address).
An unchanged event is published when the inbound directory message produced no changes in the graph. Consumers implementing reconciliation logic can use it to confirm that the structure is still active.
A deleted event signals that the structure has been removed from the graph. Consumers should treat subsequent references to its uid as invalid.
